# Byteman rule for the held-heap reading (design R5, O2). @FLAG@ is replaced by run.sh with the flag file's path.
# While the flag file exists, a request whose partition key is the int 424242 waits 15 s at ResultSetBuilder.newRow,
# which SelectStatement.processPartition calls right after partition.next() has built the row (SelectStatement.java:1125-1126),
# so the materialized row is live while run.sh takes a forced-GC class histogram. Other requests are not affected.
# Shakedown fix S1 (2026-11-17): `new X(..).m()` does not parse inside IF, so the flag File is bound with BIND.
RULE s4 hold coordinator row at newRow
CLASS org.apache.cassandra.cql3.selection.ResultSetBuilder
METHOD newRow
AT ENTRY
BIND flag : java.io.File = new java.io.File("@FLAG@")
IF $2.getKey().remaining() == 4 && $2.getKey().getInt($2.getKey().position()) == 424242 && flag.exists()
DO traceln("S4PAUSE begin " + java.lang.System.currentTimeMillis());
   waitFor("s4-never-signalled", 15000L);
   traceln("S4PAUSE end " + java.lang.System.currentTimeMillis())
ENDRULE
